lesson k-hello-and-colours v=1 format=teach grade=0 unit=3 subject=language levels=[easy, medium, hard] {
  title "[[greet.hello|cap]] and [[colour.red]]"
  goal "Say [[greet.hello]] and [[greet.goodbye]] at the right moment, and name four colours in [[language.name]]."

  look {
    scene 30x7 {
      mixingtray paints wells=["red", "blue", "yellow", "green"] labels=true at=canvas(1, 1)
    }
    say """
      In [[language.name]] we say [[greet.hello]] when we arrive and [[greet.goodbye]] when we go.
      Red is [[colour.red]], blue is [[colour.blue]], yellow is [[colour.yellow]] and green is
      [[colour.green]]. Say each one aloud after a grown-up.
      """
  }
  do {
    level easy {
      worked k.lang-hello-or-goodbye k=0 level=medium
    }
    practice k.lang-hello-or-goodbye count=2 seed=2
    practice k.lang-what-it-means count=2 seed=3 easy-count=1
    practice k.lang-colour-name count=2 seed=4
    practice k.lang-find-the-paint count=2 seed=5
    show k.lang-say-hello
  }
  try stars=2 {
    show k.lang-thank-you k=0 hard-k=1
  }
  try stars=3 {
    show k.lang-mix k=0 hard-k=1
  }
  remember {
    say "[[greet.hello|cap]] to come and [[greet.goodbye]] to go. Red is [[colour.red]] and blue is [[colour.blue]]."
  }

  grown-ups """
    Everything here is heard: read the words aloud, [[greet.hello]] said [[greet.hello|say]] and
    [[greet.goodbye]] said [[greet.goodbye|say]], and let the child say them back. The child picks
    from what you read, so nothing needs to be read by the child. The talking question is for you to
    listen to. If the child is stuck, act it out: walk in and say [[greet.hello]], walk out and say
    [[greet.goodbye]]. Off the page, name the colours of the fruit bowl in the language at breakfast.
    Japan, 幼稚園教育要領 (kindergarten guidelines), 言葉, 内容 (7): "生活の中で言葉の楽しさや美しさに気付く。"
    (Notice the fun and beauty of words in daily life.) The phrases are in [[language.variety]].
    """
  level easy {
    grown-ups "At this level coming in is worked in the teacher's pen first, the colours are red and blue, and the two-star is thank you."
  }
  level hard {
    grown-ups "At this level the words to know include [[greet.please]] and [[greet.thank-you]], the colours are yellow and green, and the three-star mix is orange."
  }
}
